-- title:
--   Centre-pinned specialisation of places on the finite j-chart
-- statement:
--   Fix $p\ge 1$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid p$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $\ell$ (that is, $\ell$ is a nonunit of $A$) whose residue field $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $\ell$; let $\rho$ be a ring homomorphism from the subring $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}\subset\mathbb{Q}$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$ into $A$ compatible with the inclusion $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Suppose given, for every nonzero divisor $d$ of $p$, modular polynomial data $\Phi_d\in\mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ (monic of degree $\psi(d)$ and vanishing at $(j,j_d)$), with the reduction of $\Phi_p$ modulo $\ell$ separable over $\kappa(X)$, and assume $\kappa(\tilde\jmath,\tilde\jmath_p)=\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,p$ coincides with $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,\kappa\,p$, the subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by all $q$-expansions $\tilde\jmath_d$, $d\mid p$ (hypothesis $hCF$). Let $fm$ be a fibre model of level $p$ at $A$ with residue map $\mathrm{residue}:A\to\kappa$, possessing a cusp chart, whose finite subring $B_{\mathrm{fin}}$ contains the image under the coefficient embedding of every element of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,p\,\ell$ (the elements of the full modular function field integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j]$) and whose subring $B_\infty$ contains the image of every element of $\mathrm{chartAlgInf}\,p\,\ell$ (integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j^{-1}]$). Let $w$ be a place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(X_0(p))=\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,p$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $v$ be a place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,\kappa\,p$ over $\kappa$, and let $\alpha:\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,p\,\ell\to A$ be a ring homomorphism such that, for every $b$ in $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,p\,\ell$: the image of $b$ lies in the valuation subring of $w$ and $b-\alpha(b)$ lies in its nonunits; and the image of $fm.piFin(b)$ in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,\kappa\,p$ lies in the valuation subring of $v$ and differs from $\mathrm{residue}(\alpha(b))$ by a nonunit of it. Then $v$ is the transport along the ring isomorphism $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,p\cong\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFullC}\,\kappa\,p$ furnished by $hCF$ (comap along its inverse) of the place $fm.\mathrm{spPlace}(w)$ obtained from $w$ by the fibre model's specialisation of places, built from the surjectivity of the residue map, the data $\Phi_d$ and the separability hypothesis.
--
--   This is the finite-chart, scheme-free core of the statement that reduction of an $A$-valued point of the modular curve is compatible with specialisation of places: once the two places $w$ and $v$ are pinned to the generic and special centres of one and the same $A$-point $\alpha$ of the $j$-finite chart, they correspond under the fibre model's specialisation map. It is used by [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.pointReduction_eq_congr_spPlace_of_cuspChart_centrePin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.pointReduction_eq_congr_spPlace_of_cuspChart_centrePin), where the hypotheses are produced from an $A$-point of the Igusa scheme factoring through the finite chart.
